// New Mexico OSE code tables.
//
// Unlike every other state in this project, these were NOT reverse-engineered
// from sample data — the Office of the State Engineer publishes an official
// data dictionary, and this file is generated straight from it:
//   https://www.ose.nm.gov/GIS/PODS/nmose_WATERS_PODs_data_dictionary_v8.xlsx
//   (linked from the OSE's own ArcGIS item for the POD layer)
//
// That matters because it's the difference between decoding and guessing.
// Nevada's equivalent work left 10 of 24 status codes raw for want of an
// authoritative source; here every code below is the agency's own wording.
//
// Regenerate by re-downloading the dictionary and re-running the extraction
// if OSE publishes a v9.

